{# PL·A4 "Observations awaiting action" — and the honest version of it.

   THE DESIGN ASKS FOR A NUMBER THIS MODULE DOES NOT HOLD. Its card is headed "18
   unfiled · oldest first" and offers a "File as incident →" on every row. This
   module cannot know which observations have been filed: the incidents module
   records the observation's uuid on ITS side (Incident::sourceRecordUuid) and
   nothing on this side mirrors it.

   So there is no unfiled count and no unfiled filter here. Showing every
   observation as unfiled would be worse than showing none — it would be a queue
   of invented work somebody would sit down and work through. What the card does
   instead is what it can prove: the area's latest observations, oldest first,
   with their real age, the patrol they were logged on, what was seen and the
   zone the point fell in. Its own copy says the rest.

   The row's action opens the OBSERVATION rather than filing it, for the same
   reason: a "file as incident" link would have to name another module's route,
   and this module names no other module. #}
{% set pl = by.patrols %}
{% set q = pl.observations %}
<div class="c" data-w="pl_obsq">
    <span class="tab"><span class="idx">PL·A4</span>Observations awaiting action<span class="src">· oldest first · the latest {{ q.rows|length }}</span></span>
    <span class="ao-by patrols"><i></i>patrols</span>
    <div class="use patrol-ao-lead">An observation is <b>not</b> an incident. Most stay notes; these are the ones somebody has to decide about. Whether one has already been <b>filed as an incident is not recorded on this side</b> — the incidents module holds that link — so this card counts no queue and marks nothing as unfiled.</div>

    {% if q.rows|length %}
        <table class="tbl">
            <tr>
                <th>obs</th>
                <th>patrol</th>
                <th>what was seen</th>
                <th>zone</th>
                <th class="patrol-right">age</th>
                <th></th>
            </tr>
            {% for row in q.rows %}
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="mono patrol-ref">{{ row.observation.ref }}</span></td>
                    <td><a href="{{ row.patrolUrl }}">{{ row.observation.patrol.ref }}</a></td>
                    <td>{{ row.category }}{% if row.observation.note %} — {{ row.observation.note }}{% endif %}</td>
                    {# An unpositioned observation is given no zone rather than a
                       guess; the field app may sync one on purpose. #}
                    <td class="fog">{{ row.zone ?: '—' }}</td>
                    <td class="num">
                        {% if row.ageLabel is null %}
                            <span class="chip idle">not timed</span>
                        {% else %}
                            <span class="chip {{ row.ageSeconds >= 432000 ? 'fail' : (row.ageSeconds >= 172800 ? 'warn' : 'idle') }}">{{ row.ageLabel }}</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </td>
                    <td class="patrol-right"><a class="open-btn" href="{{ row.url }}">Open →</a></td>
                </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </table>

        <div class="rln patrol-ao-foot">
            <span class="fog">Logged this month</span>
            <span class="mono patrol-ao-mono">{{ q.monthCount }} · each keeps its patrol id</span>
        </div>
    {% else %}
        <p class="patrol-empty">No observations have been logged in this area yet.</p>
    {% endif %}
</div>
